    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class \u2014 the only one in the repo).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a created owner's response include `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names. I implemented this by keeping each piece of logic where it belongs:\n\n1. **API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 Added a `displayName` `readOnly` string property to the `Owner` schema. It's read-only (computed/derived, never accepted as input), so it lives on `Owner` rather than the editable `OwnerFields`. The build regenerates `OwnerDto` with the matching field.\n\n2. **Domain logic** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 Added a `@Transient` computed getter `getDisplayName()` that returns `getLastName() + \", \" + getFirstName()`. The formatting logic sits on the entity that owns the names, reusing the inherited `Person` accessors rather than duplicating name handling elsewhere.\n\n3. **Mapping** \u2014 No change needed: MapStruct's existing `toOwnerDto` auto-maps the matching `displayName` property, so no bespoke wiring accumulated in the mapper. The reverse `toOwner` mapping ignores it since `Owner` has no `displayName` setter.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreComputesDisplayName`) and the full suite pass.",
